  "claims": [
    "clean Node-only repository: canonical source, tests, examples, setup, MIT license and application-linked architecture/handoff",
    "previously implemented exact augmented AVL, transactional integrity and reactive settlement pass fresh migrated verification",
    "private-by-default explicit resource access orders with dedicated model/membership views and trusted owner-header partition role, including composite partitions",
    "pure fixture principal-DAG preparation, canonical identity, configurable graph budgets and per-actor scope without all-pairs descendant closure",
    "owner-only action semantics mirror native policy: self/descendants/direct Group parents, narrower Delete, direct active Group/Tenant raw-grant inheritance only for Users, admin neither widens owners nor implicitly grants Use",
    "one active User effective administrator retained; malformed graphs reject; handles and fixture input are detached/frozen",
    "declarative reference examples demonstrate incoming indexes, 1:N, uniqueness-backed at-most-one 1:1, and N:M junctions with two derived reverse entries",
    "next implementation obligations preserved in self-contained local docs with pinned optional predecessor sources"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "fixture authority functions are not wired into mutations or reads; raw engine APIs remain trusted",
    "hydrated authorized owner-stream merge, authorized mutations/reference reads, explicit anchor-summary disclosure and fenced cursors remain open",
    "index lifecycle and adaptive population/workload tools remain JS-P5; no full workbench or production readiness claim",
    "only a serialized volatile memory adapter is supplied; persistent KV adapters, distributed concurrency, receipts, identity/network, services and deployment need independent gates",
    "memory reverse-reference scans enumerate the store; existing metadata is not yet a supported authorized reverse-query API",
    "scalar reference plus uniqueness guarantees at most one, not mandatory existence in both directions",
    "pure authority handles do not track revocation/current sessions; future wrappers must load current authority inside transaction scope",
    "logical read-byte budgets are post-fetch and are not hard heap/transfer caps",
    "no Rust code, native storage stores, credentials, caches or historical acceptance binaries migrated"
  ],
